28:16.772 --> 28:20.352
Meaning that your other sales tax bondholders would get paid

28:20.384 --> 28:23.965
first, and any other bonds that you put on parity

28:23.981 --> 28:27.931
with that would get paid first. And from the

28:28.075 --> 28:31.318
remaining sales tax revenue, you would pay any

28:31.383 --> 28:35.076
shortfall from that other from the from the subset

28:35.576 --> 28:39.234
area of this development. So with

28:39.734 --> 28:42.782
that, then quantitatively on page the bottom of page. 3.

28:43.569 --> 28:47.003
You can see the options laid out with what the construction fund—

28:47.019 --> 28:50.453
I mean, construction funds are the same across the board, that $8 million I mentioned.

28:51.432 --> 28:55.476
In some of the structures, in the TIF-only structure

28:55.685 --> 28:59.087
and the moral obligation structure,

28:59.392 --> 29:02.522
there's still enough of a risk that we would want to— for the

29:03.022 --> 29:07.015
