30:17.006 --> 30:20.151
the, you know, bettering of the credit, so to speak, for those reasons.

30:20.697 --> 30:23.987
The amortization is the same straight across. I anticipate

30:24.487 --> 30:28.384
the rating to be non-rated on option 1, middle of the road on

30:28.884 --> 30:32.460
option A+ to AA- with a subordinate sales

30:32.493 --> 30:36.039
tax pledge. I think it will be

30:36.248 --> 30:40.067
a little bit less than your current regular sales tax bonds

30:40.567 --> 30:44.256
because these are subordinate to that. You see the difference in interest rates

30:44.512 --> 30:47.818
as a TIF pledge only about— I'm guessing in today's market would

30:48.318 --> 30:51.541
be about at a 6.20. On the other option,

30:52.151 --> 30:55.537
the bookends, so to speak, I think we could get a subordinate

30:56.037 --> 30:58.936
sales sales tax done at about a 4.12% over that 15 years.

30:59.753 --> 31:04.145
You see the differentials in average annual payment. On the high end, it's $930,000

31:04.645 --> 31:08.874
