03:13:16.863 --> 03:13:19.299
might— for the public. So basically,

03:13:20.277 --> 03:13:23.792
The code, other than defining where this— the first part defines

03:13:23.984 --> 03:13:27.322
which properties it would apply to, and basically it would have

03:13:27.435 --> 03:13:30.933
a 30-foot setback for primary structures,

03:13:31.511 --> 03:13:34.768
and then there is that they could apply

03:13:35.940 --> 03:13:41.332
for an exception. And mainly this will impact R-1

03:13:41.832 --> 03:13:45.536
and smaller for rear setbacks. It's really only

03:13:45.552 --> 03:13:48.693
a corner property it might do a side setback.

03:13:48.936 --> 03:13:52.666
They'd have to have more property on the side of their lots.

03:13:52.747 --> 03:13:56.605
But larger lots have 35 rear setbacks

03:13:56.685 --> 03:14:01.105
