03:14:01.605 --> 03:14:05.272
accessory dwellings— accessory buildings,

03:14:05.482 --> 03:14:08.945
it would also have a 30-foot setback for those. Again,

03:14:08.961 --> 03:14:11.938
you could, if your shed's smaller than 200 feet,

03:14:12.302 --> 03:14:16.222
it wouldn't impact you. So it's only if it's above 200 or

03:14:16.722 --> 03:14:20.206
has like electrical and plumbing. So, and, and then the

03:14:20.495 --> 03:14:25.364
Planning Commission, they recommended having those accessory

03:14:25.862 --> 03:14:29.573
buildings in it as well, accessory structures. And Council

03:14:30.073 --> 03:14:33.461
Member Wright, just curious, some of our other exceptions, if you will,

03:14:33.911 --> 03:14:36.465
are actually decisions made at Planning Commission.

03:14:37.188 --> 03:14:40.501
But if the exceptions are built into this for places like Circle 5 that

03:14:41.001 --> 03:14:44.977
says, hey, this is our suggested rules,

03:14:45.026 --> 03:14:49.346
if you will, but just like a mitigation plan for

03:14:49.846 --> 03:14:53.737
other codes, if they could come with some kind of plan

03:14:54.237 --> 03:14:57.996
or exception, request for exception, that it's easily mitigated,

03:14:58.675 --> 03:15:01.019
