03:44:47.715 --> 03:44:50.539
be existing in a regular neighborhood. Yes.

03:44:50.587 --> 03:44:53.782
Because they could— the next person can come in and not have it be senior

03:44:54.282 --> 03:44:59.402
housing if it's done in that regard. So then it stops meeting the purpose that

03:44:59.902 --> 03:45:01.222
we did it in the first place. And you can disagree with that, but I

03:45:01.722 --> 03:45:05.308
just think if we're going to do it, it needs to be specific. It should

03:45:05.357 --> 03:45:08.998
probably be a gated community if we're talking about twin

03:45:09.498 --> 03:45:13.156
homes, fourplexes. All need to be single level,

03:45:13.510 --> 03:45:17.105
no stacked single houses,

03:45:17.363 --> 03:45:20.168
any of those things. They all need to be patio-type homes.

03:45:21.843 --> 03:45:23.360
But they don't want to take care of their property. I think that's a good

03:45:23.860 --> 03:45:26.320
point. Why is that a requirement? I'm getting pretty close to 55. I can still

03:45:26.820 --> 03:45:29.640
walk upstairs. I'm just throwing that out there. I mean, I've seen Brett go upstairs.

03:45:30.420 --> 03:45:35.240
Yeah, I'm going to tell you, when people are going—

03:45:35.740 --> 03:45:38.000
I can promise you, when you get to that point, Jared, the last thing you're

03:45:38.500 --> 03:45:40.760
going to want to do with your back is going up and down the stairs.

03:45:41.260 --> 03:45:42.960
And your wife's going to say, enough, I don't want to see you fall down

03:45:43.460 --> 03:45:47.140
the stairs. But I'm going to tell you, I come from that community of

03:45:47.640 --> 03:45:51.396
geriatric care. They're looking to prevent

03:45:51.525 --> 03:45:55.475
slips and falls that generally end up in hip

03:45:55.523 --> 03:45:59.409
breaking and things of that nature. So stairs is bad for

03:45:59.909 --> 03:46:02.588
the senior community, and most of them are looking to get away from that because

03:46:02.652 --> 03:46:05.960
they don't feel stable on the stairs. So I just— if we're

03:46:06.460 --> 03:46:09.942
going to do it, what incentivizes them? They don't want to take care of

03:46:09.974 --> 03:46:13.506
the property, so it needs to be something that's enclosed, so somebody else

03:46:14.006 --> 03:46:17.071
is taking care of it. I think for For me, that's what I'm looking for

03:46:17.119 --> 03:46:19.881
out of this. I don't care if it's an overlay zone, but it needs to

03:46:19.913 --> 03:46:22.980
have some better guardrails, in my opinion. Okay,

03:46:23.220 --> 03:46:27.203
because the overlay would be an easier mechanism to work in some

03:46:27.235 --> 03:46:30.221
of those incentives because it's a whole chapter of code.

03:46:31.008 --> 03:46:34.075
So it gives us more room to play with to add things into that.

03:46:34.123 --> 03:46:36.933
Yeah, so I don't think it's a zone. I think perhaps it's an overlay.

03:46:37.254 --> 03:46:41.292
And I mean, another strategy in my mind is to consider doing

03:46:41.792 --> 03:46:44.130
